
=== prefab_side_generic
" Generic definition of a Side. If a side has enemies or allies, the side will be added to the enemy/ally list for 
" the applicable sides. Defaults are the TSN values.
metadata: ```
type: prefab/side
name: TSN
key: tsn
desc:
allies:
enemies:
races: terran
color: #000FFF
icon_index:
```
    if key is None:
        # key is the only critical property
        yield fail
    # Re-declaring a side CONVERGES, it does not fail. side_create reconfigures an
    # existing side in place (one agent per key, via side_ensure) and re-issues every
    # engine write, which makes a second call a REPAIR rather than an error -- and that
    # repair is required, not merely tolerated: sim_create() leaves the sim handle stale
    # for the rest of the frame, so relations/colors written in that frame land on a
    # discarded simulation and only a later re-declare restores them.
    #
    # This used to `yield fail` when the key already existed, which made the prefab
    # disagree with side_create / sides_declare / a2x_declare_sides (all idempotent) and
    # turned the ordinary "declare my sides again" repair into a failed prefab.
    id = side_create(key, name, desc, color, icon_index, races, allies, enemies)
    yield result id
    ->END
